    "summary": "This 2014 Pagani Huayra is the 71st of 100 coupes built between 2011 and 2018 and is a US-specification example that was sold new via Aston Martin of Dallas. After being purchased by the seller in 2023, the car was reportedly sent back to Pagani in 2025 for installation of the Tempesta package, which added a titanium exhaust system, Öhlins coilovers, 20” and 21” staggered-width wheels, and a revised front splitter, underbody panels, and rear diffuser constructed from carbon fiber. Featuring a carbon-titanium monocoque wrapped in dark-blue-painted carbon-fiber bodywork, the car is powered by a 6.0-liter Mercedes-AMG M158 V12 that features twin turbochargers and dry-sump lubrication. Additional features include an Xtrac transverse seven-speed automated manual transaxle with a single clutch as well as pushrod-operated adjustable coilover suspension, carbon-ceramic brakes, active aerodynamics, dark gray and beige washed leather upholstery, an aluminum gearshift mechanism with exposed linkage, a touchscreen infotainment system, and a Sonus Faber sound system. This Huayra has 7,700 miles and is now offered in Beverly Hills, California, with a matching fitted luggage set, owner’s manuals, a clean Carfax report, and a clean Montana title in the name of the seller’s LLC.",
